      "pilot_form_snowpack_science": "You are solid water stored on land. Warm near-snow air can melt you into liquid that follows the surface below; dry air, wind, and energy can help you sublime directly into invisible water vapour. Sublimation can occur while air is below freezing or above it. This teaching model follows one parcel and compresses the time involved.",
