      "below_18_6_moisture_the_honey_is_stabl": "Below about 18.6% moisture, honey is usually stable enough for capping. Stored sealed and dry, it can remain usable for a very long time; if it absorbs moisture, osmophilic yeasts can ferment it. Moisture control is therefore part of safe storage.",
