      "thermo_reference_body": "Warm body core",
      "thermo_reference_foot": "Cooler foot; varies",
      "thermo_reference_note": "Countercurrent heat exchange: nearby vessels carry blood in opposite directions. Heat passes from warmer blood heading toward the foot to cooler blood returning toward the body. This helps conserve body heat while allowing the feet to remain much cooler than the core.",
      "thermo_study_art_label": "Leg circulation: artery flows downward, vein flows upward. Colors show relative warmth, not oxygen content. Heat crosses between nearby vessels.",
      "thermo_study_artery_label": "Artery",
      "thermo_study_core": "From the core",
      "thermo_study_core_label": "Warm core",
      "thermo_study_core_note": "Warm arterial blood travels from the body toward the foot. The returning venous blood moves in the opposite direction.",
      "thermo_study_exchange": "Along the leg",
      "thermo_study_exchange_note": "Nearby vessels let heat pass from warmer arterial blood to cooler returning blood. The two blood streams stay separate.",
      "thermo_study_foot": "At the foot",
      "thermo_study_foot_label": "Foot",
      "thermo_study_foot_note": "Blood reaches the foot cooler than it left the body. A cooler foot has a smaller temperature difference from cold surroundings, reducing heat loss.",
      "thermo_study_intro": "Birds regulate heat through their feathers, circulation and behavior. Explore one way a warm-bodied bird can keep much colder feet.",
      "thermo_study_kicker": "FIELD STATION / HEAT EXCHANGE LAB",
      "thermo_study_lead": "Trace blood in opposite directions through a bird’s leg. Compare nearby vessels with a separated-vessel thought experiment to see where heat can go.",
      "thermo_study_legend": "Redder = warmer. Bluer = cooler. White arrows show blood flow; gold arrows show heat transfer. Colors do not show blood oxygen levels.",
      "thermo_study_mode": "Vessel comparison",
      "thermo_study_model": "A qualitative model, not a temperature or efficiency prediction. Vessel spacing is exaggerated for clarity. Real circulation and foot temperatures vary with species, weather and behavior; cold feet are not guaranteed to remain at one temperature.",
      "thermo_study_nearby": "Nearby vessels",
      "thermo_study_return": "Back to the core",
      "thermo_study_return_note": "Returning blood gains heat along the leg before it reaches the body. This conserves some of the heat that would otherwise leave through the foot.",
      "thermo_study_separate_core": "This hypothetical comparison keeps the outgoing and returning vessels apart. It is not an alternative anatomy you can switch on in a bird.",
      "thermo_study_separate_exchange": "With less nearby vessel contact in this model, less heat moves directly into the returning blood.",
      "thermo_study_separate_foot": "Warmer blood reaches the foot in this comparison. A warmer foot can lose more heat to the same cold surroundings.",
      "thermo_study_separate_return": "The returning blood receives less recovered heat along the leg. Compare its color near the core with the nearby-vessels model.",
      "thermo_study_separated": "Separated vessels",
      "thermo_study_source_circulation": "Cornell: bird circulation",
      "thermo_study_source_gulls": "Cornell: gulls and cold feet",
      "thermo_study_title": "Warm body. Cold feet. Clever plumbing.",
      "thermo_study_trace": "Trace blood and heat",
      "thermo_study_vein_label": "Vein",
      "thermo_study_window": "COUNTERCURRENT EXCHANGE",
      "trackway_constructed_direction_note": "The constructed trail advances left to right. Modeled forward toe axes point generally forward; footprint outlines and supplied sides alone do not determine a real travel history.",
      "wing3d_below_help": "Above and Below turn the camera around the same construction. Compare the flat lower slat faces with the raised upper surface and the separated tips. Selection and construction spacing stay unchanged; the section drawing below explains camber separately.",
      "wing3d_look_slots_model_yes": "Look from below: separated, upturned pieces make the tip slots visible in this construction. Compare them with the continuous outer panels of the other models. This viewer does not calculate lift or drag.",
      "wing3d_planform_nominal": "Nominal planform ratio: ",
