      "guided_memory_alternateCheckpoint": "A learner recalls where a performance took place and learns that its opening music predicts something exciting. Which explanation best fits?",
      "guided_memory_checkpoint": "A learner remembers a new classroom and later finds a familiar sound reassuring. Which explanation best fits?",
      "guided_memory_choices_0": "One region contains the entire memory and the feeling.",
      "guided_memory_choices_1": "Connected systems contribute differently to event details and learned emotional meaning.",
      "guided_memory_choices_2": "Fiber bundles create all the emotional meaning while other regions only carry messages.",
      "guided_memory_feedback_0": "Remembering and emotional learning involve distributed networks. One structure is not a complete store for the event and feeling.",
      "guided_memory_feedback_1": "Event details and learned emotional significance draw on connected systems with different contributions.",
      "guided_memory_feedback_2": "Fiber bundles carry information between structures. Emotional learning involves connected processing areas, not the bundle alone.",
      "guided_memory_hint": "Distinguish what happened and where, the routes carrying information, and why an event became important.",
      "guided_memory_inspection": "The hippocampus contributes to forming memories of experiences. The fornix carries information between connected structures. The amygdala contributes to emotional learning. Their contributions differ, and remembering also involves other brain areas.",
      "guided_memory_locations_0": "A structure deep inside the temporal lobe.",
      "guided_memory_locations_1": "A fiber bundle connecting the hippocampus with other structures.",
      "guided_memory_locations_2": "A group of nuclei near the front of the hippocampus.",
      "guided_memory_notice": "Compare a processing structure, a connecting bundle, and a contributor to emotional learning. They belong to wider networks; memories are not stored in one box.",
      "guided_memory_objective": "Compare remembering an event, carrying information between regions, and learning its emotional significance.",
      "guided_memory_prediction": "A learner remembers where a surprise party happened and why it felt exciting. Which prediction fits?",
      "guided_memory_predictions_0": "Different connected systems contribute to event details and emotional significance.",
      "guided_memory_predictions_1": "The amygdala stores every detail because the event was emotional.",
      "guided_memory_predictions_2": "A connecting fiber bundle holds the complete memory by itself.",
      "guided_memory_recap": "Memory for an experience involves connected structures and routes. Emotional significance can influence remembering, but no single region holds every detail or produces every feeling.",
      "guided_memory_reflection": "Think, say, draw, or write: Remembering details differs from …; the connecting bundle helps by … .",
      "guided_memory_title": "Remembering an experience",
