      "angle_at_support": "Angle at support",
      "apply_loads_in_the_simulation_for_phys": "Apply loads in the simulation. For physical models: weights, books, water. Where does it fail first? Why?",
      "apply_this_design_to_my_bridge": "Apply this design to my bridge",
      "arch_bridge_thrust_diagram": "Arch bridge thrust diagram",
      "arch_desc": "하중을 바깥쪽과 아래쪽의 교대로 밀어내는 곡선 구조입니다. 이상적인 하중 아래에서는 아치 자체가 거의 전적으로 압축력을 받습니다.",
      "arches_do_the_opposite_of_suspension_b": "Arches do the opposite of suspension bridges: a load on top pushes the curve OUTWARD into the abutments rather than pulling them inward. The entire arch is in compression — there is no tension in a true arch under design loads. This is why stone arches work (stone is excellent in compression). The horizontal thrust at the supports is the design challenge — abutments must resist it without sliding or tipping.",
      "avg_stay_angle_to_horiz": "Avg stay angle (to horiz.)",
      "bailey_bridge": "Bailey bridge",
      "bascule_drawbridge": "Bascule (drawbridge)",
      "base_isolation": "Base isolation: ",
      "base_isolation_2": "Base isolation",
      "beam_bending_diagram": "Beam bending diagram",
      "beam_desc": "The simplest bridge. A horizontal beam supported at each end. The beam is in compression on top and tension on bottom under load.",
      "below_the_critical_flutter_speed_moder": "Below the critical flutter speed. Modern bridges have streamlined or trussed cross-sections that prevent flutter at any wind speed they're likely to encounter. Wind tunnel testing is now mandatory for major bridges.",
      "below_the_critical_pedestrian_density_": "Below the critical pedestrian density. Random gait phasing cancels out laterally. Modern pedestrian bridges include tuned mass dampers + lateral viscous dampers to suppress this even at high density — the Millennium retrofit added ~87 dampers total.",
      "bending_stress": "Bending stress σ",
      "bending_stress_from_external_load_mpa": "Bending stress from external load (MPa)",
      "bending_stress_is_highest_at_the_top_b": "휨 응력은 중립축에서 먼 상단과 하단에서 가장 크고 중심에서는 0입니다. 따라서 단면 가운데의 재료는 낭비됩니다. I-형 단면은 재료를 휨을 담당하는 상·하부 플랜지에 집중시키고, 가운데에는 주로 전단을 담당하는 얇은 복부만 남깁니다. 같은 높이에서 같은 무게의 꽉 찬 직사각형보다 약 2배 큰 휨 내력을 얻습니다(이상적 한계에서는 3배). 갈릴레오(1638)는 속이 빈 형상이 무게 대비 더 강하다는 점에 주목했고, 정확한 보의 휨 이론은 이후 파랑, 쿨롱, 나비에에 의해 정립되었습니다.",
      "blue_compression": "blue = compression",
      "bolted_modular_connections_enable_salv": "Bolted + modular connections enable salvage at end of life. Older welded + rusted bridges get scrapped; modular ones get repurposed.",
      "boundary_conditions_the_model": "Boundary conditions = the model",
      "bridge_aesthetics_iconic_designs_throu": "🌉 Bridge aesthetics — iconic designs through history",
      "bridge_demolition_decommissioning": "💣 Bridge demolition + decommissioning",
