      "nautilus_is": "Nautilus is ",
      "nautilus_living_fossil_correction": "Cephalopod lineages extend back more than 500 million years. Living nautiluses retain an external shell, but they have continued evolving and diversifying; \"living fossil\" is shorthand, not evidence of an unchanged animal.",
      "nautilus_pathway_keeps_the_ancestral_c": "Nautilus pathway — keeps the ancestral coiled shell + most of the ancestral body plan + the ancestral pace of life. 90 tentacles with sticky pads instead of suckers.",
      "nautilus_pompilius": "Nautilus pompilius",
      "nautilus_pompilius_vision": "Nautilus pompilius vision",
      "nautilus_shell_can_withstand_pressures": "Experiments on living nautiluses found their shells imploding at depths of about 785 to 830 m (Kanie & Hattori 1983), so shell strength sets how deep a nautilus can live.",
      "nautilus_shell_trade": "Nautilus Shell Trade",
      "nautilus_shells_are_divided_into_chamb": "Nautilus shells are divided into chambers connected by a tube called the siphuncle. By pumping fluid through it, the animal adjusts buoyancy.",
      "nautiluses_were_cites_listed_in_2017_o": "Nautiluses were CITES-listed in 2017 — over a decade after population declines started. Why does conservation often lag behind scientific evidence?",
