      "3_142_distracted_driving_deaths_in_the": ". At 55 mph, NHTSA compares that to driving a football-field length blind. Talking on a handheld phone roughly quadruples your crash risk — but TEXTING is in a different category again: a Virginia Tech study of truck drivers put it near 23×, because it takes your eyes, hands, and attention at the same time. NHTSA also reports 3,208 distracted-driving deaths and 315,167 injuries in 2024.",
