      "black_ice_forms_between_28_f_and_38_f_": "Black ice is most slippery when the temperature is near freezing, because the ice is wet. Expect it at or below 32°F, and stay alert when your car's thermometer reads a few degrees above that: the road can be colder than the air. Bridges and overpasses freeze first and dry out last (Maine driver's manual). Also watch shaded curves and pre-dawn hours. The surface looks wet, not icy.",
