      "start_function_sleuth": "Start Function Sleuth",
      "start_over": "↻ Run it again",
      "start_the_drill": "▶ Start the drill",
      "sticker": "Sticker",
      "tangible": "Tangible",
      "tk_balance": "Token balance",
      "tk_build_h": "🛠️ Build one",
      "tk_build_sub": "Award tokens, then spend them. Watch the exchange ratio: a menu whose cheapest item takes a week to reach is a menu the student stops working for.",
      "tk_earn": "Earn tokens",
      "tk_footer": "🪙 A token economy is a scaffold, not a destination. The plan should name from the start how the schedule thins, what natural reinforcer takes over, and how you would know it had.",
      "tk_log": "Exchange record",
      "tk_part1": "1. What earns a token",
      "tk_part1_b": "Specific, observable, and already within reach. If the student cannot yet do it, a token system will not teach it — that is a job for instruction and shaping first.",
      "tk_part2": "2. The token itself",
      "tk_part2_b": "Delivered immediately, visibly, and without negotiation. Its value is entirely borrowed from the exchange, which is why an exchange that keeps slipping kills the system.",
      "tk_part3": "3. Backup reinforcers",
      "tk_part3_b": "Chosen by the student, not the adult. A reinforcer is defined by its effect on behaviour — if the behaviour does not increase, the thing on the menu is not a reinforcer, however much you would like it to be.",
      "tk_pit1": "Paying for what the student already does reliably. That is not reinforcement, it is a wage — and it can reduce the behaviour once the wage stops.",
      "tk_pit2": "An exchange ratio nobody can reach. If the cheapest item is days away, the token stops predicting anything and stops working.",
      "tk_pit3": "Taking tokens away. Response cost is a punishment procedure with its own ethical and procedural requirements; bolting it onto an earn-only board is a change of intervention, not a tweak.",
      "tk_pit4": "No plan to end. A board that never thins toward natural reinforcers is a board the student needs forever, which was never the goal.",
      "tk_pit5": "A menu the adult picked. Preference is measured, not assumed — and it changes week to week.",
      "tk_pitfalls_h": "⚠️ Where token boards go wrong",
      "tk_reset": "Reset the token board",
      "tk_reset_label": "↻ Reset board",
      "tk_spend": "Exchange",
      "token_economy_h": "🪙 Token economy",
      "token_economy_sub": "Tokens are conditioned reinforcers: worthless in themselves, valuable because of what they buy. Three parts have to be designed together — the behaviours that earn, the token, and the backup reinforcers it exchanges for.",
      "token_economy_tab": "Token Economy",
      "vignette": "Vignette",
      "12_sections_4_interactive": "12 sections · 4 interactive",
      "9_progressive_levels_schedule_sleuth_f": "9 progressive levels · Schedule Sleuth · Function Sleuth · Glossary · Ethics",
