      "arc_target_speed": "Target travel speed",
      "arc_tn_ext": "Run three hands-on passes at the same target speed and record uniformity each time: does practice tighten the trace? Then, if your shop can section and etch a practice coupon under instructor supervision, compare its profile with the macro-etch panel and list which settings you would change to match it. Model numbers here are representative classroom values, not a welding procedure.",
      "arc_tn_m1": "\"Amps, volts and speed all do the same thing\" — they don't. Amperage sets how much metal melts and how deep; voltage sets how wide and flat it spreads; travel speed sets how much of both lands on each inch.",
      "arc_tn_m2": "\"More penetration is always better\" — the target is specified. Past the root is burn-through, and extra heat grows distortion and the heat-affected zone.",
      "arc_tn_m3": "\"A smooth-looking bead is a sound bead\" — lack of fusion is mostly below the surface. Only a cut and etch, a bend test, or ultrasound finds it.",
      "arc_tn_m4": "\"Heat tint means the weld is bad\" — temper colours on carbon steel are a thin surface oxide and normal. On stainless, heavy tint lowers corrosion resistance, so it is usually removed.",
      "arc_tn_m5": "\"Aluminum is easier than steel because it's softer\" — its conductivity, oxide layer and lack of glow before melting make it harder to weld.",
      "arc_tn_q1": "Pin the default bead, then change ONLY travel speed. Which numbers changed, and which stayed almost the same? Why does the toe angle barely move while the width does?",
      "arc_tn_q2": "Lay a hands-on pass and read the speed trace. Where the trace dips, what happened to the bead width and ripple spacing on the plate? Explain it with heat input per inch.",
      "arc_tn_q3": "Why does the scorecard reject a bead with a burn-through hole even when its penetration and uniformity rows look good?",
      "arc_tn_q4": "The macro-etch shows a heat-affected zone outside the fusion line. What changed in that metal even though it never melted?",
      "arc_tn_q5": "Switch from mild steel to aluminum without changing voltage or amperage. What happens to penetration and to the heat tint? Why?",
