      "cons8_identification_heading_r2": "Tungsten electrodes — painted identification end",
      "cons8_intro": "Select a reference electrode, then inspect its identification end, package designation or grinding direction. Color names and classifications stay readable below the drawing.",
      "cons8_model_note": "Schematic references on the same scale. The rod, box and grinding marks stay fixed; only the selected identification information and outline change. No electrode size, tip angle, machine setting or weld-quality prediction is shown.",
      "cons8_paint_caption": "The painted end is an identification cue. Read its color name together with the printed classification and product instructions.",
      "cons8_peer_label": "Comparison classification",
      "cons8_prep_caption": "The four lines run lengthwise, parallel to the rod. They locate the grinding direction; their spacing and the flat-ended rod do not specify a prepared tip shape.",
      "cons8_product_identification_r2": "Tungsten color codes depend on the applicable standard edition and product. Current manufacturer charts list EWCe-2/WC20 as gray (formerly orange); EWG blends can use maker-specific colors. Read the printed classification and the electrode manufacturer’s instructions instead of identifying an electrode by paint alone.",
      "cons8_reference": "Read all nine reference entries",
      "cons8_reference_box": "REFERENCE BOX",
      "cons8_reference_intro_r2": "Select a reference electrode to inspect its printed classification and identification color. Color names accompany every reference.",
