      "insp2_rt_aria": "RT demo: a crack tilted {value1} degrees from the beam. The beam passes through {value2} in of it, {value3}% of the wall, so the film {value4}.",
      "insp2_rt_cap": "Lined up with the beam, the crack removes its full height of metal from the beam path and prints a dark line. Tilt it and the beam crosses only the thin opening, so the line fades fast. This is why RT misses planar flaws at the bevel angle and why UT complements it.",
      "insp2_rt_invis": "too faint to show",
      "insp2_rt_legend": "Simplified model: crack 1/4 in tall and 0.004 in open in a 1/2 in wall. It shows when the beam path through it is at least about 2% of the wall, a typical radiographic sensitivity. F = film.",
      "insp2_rt_misses": "misses it",
      "insp2_rt_path": "Beam path through the crack",
      "insp2_rt_pct": "Share of the 1/2 in wall",
      "insp2_rt_shows": "shows it",
      "insp2_rt_tilt": "Crack tilt from the beam",
      "insp2_rt_vis": "shows on the film",
      "insp2_running": "Running total from the start: {value1}",
      "insp2_s_amps": "Run at 135 A on a WPS that lists 120-150 A.",
      "insp2_s_amps_w": "Within range. The WPS gives a range and the PQR supports it; changing amperage inside the range is what the range is for. Going outside it would mean revising the WPS, and under toughness rules possibly a new PQR.",
      "insp2_s_best": "★ Best choice",
      "insp2_s_dia": "Use 1/8 in electrodes on a WPS that lists 3/32 to 5/32 in.",
      "insp2_s_dia_w": "Within range. A diameter inside the WPS range is compliant, and for most processes electrode diameter is a nonessential variable anyway.",
      "insp2_s_fno": "Change the filler from E7018 (F-No. 4) to E6010 (F-No. 3).",
      "insp2_s_fno_w": "Requalify. The filler F-Number is an essential variable for an ASME IX procedure (QW-404.4). F-Numbers group electrodes by how they run, and moving between groups changes how the weld behaves, so the WPS needs a PQR welded with the new group.",
      "insp2_s_gas": "Switch the GMAW shielding gas from 75% argon / 25% CO2 to 100% CO2.",
      "insp2_s_gas_w": "Requalify. For GMAW and GTAW, changing the shielding gas or its mix is an essential variable (ASME IX QW-408.2), and D1.1 lists gas changes among its essential variables for qualified WPSs too. Gas changes the arc, the penetration and the weld chemistry.",
      "insp2_s_no": "✗ Will not work",
      "insp2_s_ok": "✓ Works",
      "insp2_s_pno": "Use a carbon-steel WPS (P-No. 1) to weld 304 stainless (P-No. 8).",
      "insp2_s_pno_w": "Requalify. Base metal P-Number is an essential variable (ASME IX QW-403.11). Stainless needs different filler, shielding and heat control, so it needs its own PQR.",
      "insp2_s_pos": "ASME IX job: weld overhead with a procedure whose PQR coupon was welded flat.",
      "insp2_s_pos_w": "Within range for the PROCEDURE: ASME IX says a procedure qualified in any position qualifies all positions unless notch-toughness rules apply (QW-203). The trap: the WELDER still needs a performance qualification (WPQ) that covers overhead.",
      "insp2_s_process": "Change from GMAW (solid wire) to FCAW (flux-cored wire).",
      "insp2_s_process_w": "Requalify. Each welding process needs its own qualification: a different arc, different shielding and different weld metal. A WPS covers only the process or processes its PQR proved.",
      "insp2_s_speed": "Travel at 12 in/min on a WPS that lists 8-14 in/min.",
      "insp2_s_speed_w": "Within range. Speed inside the WPS range is compliant. Speed still changes the heat put into each inch, which is why the range exists.",
      "insp2_s_thick": "Weld 1-1/2 in plate with a WPS qualified on a 3/8 in test coupon.",
      "insp2_s_thick_w": "Requalify. Under ASME IX a 3/8 in coupon qualifies base metal only up to 2T = 3/4 in (QW-451.1), and D1.1's thickness limits for that coupon also stop well short of 1-1/2 in. Thicker plate cools faster and needs its own proof.",
      "insp2_s_transfer": "Change GMAW from spray transfer to short-circuit transfer.",
      "insp2_s_transfer_w": "Requalify. Under ASME IX, switching GMAW between spray, globular or pulsed transfer and short-circuiting is essential (QW-409.2). Short-circuit runs colder and is prone to lack of fusion on thick plate.",
      "insp2_s_weak": "△ Weak here",
      "insp2_score_line": "Correct calls: {value1} of {value2} decided · Critical reading recorded before deciding: {value3} of {value2}",
      "insp2_sec_aria": "Cross-section of the weld at {value1}: {value2}.",
      "insp2_sec_legend": "Cross-section at the gauge, magnified. The yellow gauge sits on the weld exactly as drawn; the number is what it reads.",
      "insp2_slider_aria": "Gauge position along the weld. Arrow keys move 1/4 in, Shift+arrow 1 in, Enter records the reading.",
      "insp2_slider_vt": "{value1} along the weld: {value2}",
      "insp2_sort_aria": "Sort this change",
      "insp2_sort_done": "All {value1} cards sorted: {value2} right. The pattern: anything that changes the metal, the process, the filler group, the gas or the heat treatment needs proof; moving around inside a listed range does not.",
      "insp2_sort_h": "🗂 Essential Variable Sorter",
      "insp2_sort_intro": "Each card is a change a shop wants to make. Does it change an essential variable (a new PQR or requalified WPS is needed), or does it stay inside what the WPS already allows? Feedback cites the idea, mostly from ASME IX, the most explicit code on this; D1.1 and API 1104 keep their own tables, so always check the governing code.",
      "insp2_sort_reset": "🔄 Reset sorter",
