      "run_tip_clean": "{value1}% of the bead in spec. Try the next tier: a tighter band and bigger disturbances.",
      "run_tip_ctwd_long": "While your stickout drifted long at {value1} in., the arc lost up to about {value2} A and only {value3}% stayed in spec. Nudge the amps up or slow a little; in the booth you would also bring the torch back down.",
      "run_tip_ctwd_short": "When your stickout got short at {value1} in., the arc gained up to about {value2} A and only {value3}% stayed in spec. Ease the amps down or speed up a little.",
      "run_tip_gap": "Over the fit-up gap at {value1} in., only {value2}% of the bead stayed in spec. With less metal under the arc it digs deeper: speed up or lower the amps across a gap.",
      "run_tip_heat": "The plate climbed to {value1} °F and the last quarter of the bead ran deep. A long joint heats up: ease the travel speed up as you go.",
      "run_tip_jerky": "Your bead width wandered (uniformity {value1}%). Make small, early corrections instead of big, late ones.",
      "run_tip_step_good": "You crossed the thickness step cleanly (back in spec within {value1} in.). That is reading the joint ahead of the puddle.",
      "run_tip_step_late": "When the plate thinned at {value1} in., it took {value2} in. of travel to get back in spec. Watch the step line ahead and start speeding up as the puddle reaches it.",
      "run_tip_step_never": "After the plate thinned at {value1} in., the bead never came back into spec. Thin plate needs about half the heat per inch: speed up or turn the amps down as the puddle reaches the step line.",
      "run_tip_tack": "Crossing the tack weld at {value1} in., only {value2}% stayed in spec. The tack soaks up heat: slow down briefly to fuse into it.",
      "run_tips_h": "Coaching",
