      "fig_hl_aria": "Reseeding a reef in three steps. On a spawning night, scientists collected millions of coral larvae. They released them under net tents on a damaged Philippine reef. Most died, as wild coral babies do, but within two to three years about 220 grew into corals big enough to spawn, starting a new breeding group.",
