      "fig_hs_above": "Seen from above.",
      "fig_hs_aria": "Three views of the sea floor from above. Loose rubble left alone stayed near 3% coral after 17 years. Divers pin the rubble under a linked web of six-sided, sand-coated steel Reef Stars and tie small corals onto them, starting at about 17% coral cover. Four years later the frames are overgrown, at about 56%. Most of the new corals are branching corals that bleach easily.",
